# Slash-less on purpose: `node_modules/` matches only a DIRECTORY, so a
# worktree that reaches its dependencies through a SYMLINK named
# `node_modules` (the PTY-provider setup) was never ignored at all — and one
# such link, whose target is an absolute machine-local path, reached a
# commit. Without the slash this rule covers both shapes.
node_modules
.superpowers/
.remember/
.claude/
.codex/
.agents/
DESIGN-IS-*/
docs/superpowers/
dist/
.routercode/
.ai-collab/
.worktrees/
.env
*.log
*.jpg
*.png
!.env.example
.DS_Store

# The desktop shell (gui/).
# `dist/` above already covers the WebView bundle; these are the rest.
gui/src-tauri/target/
gui/src-tauri/gen/
# The staged runtime `npm run gui:package` builds into the bundle: a node
# binary, dist/, and production node_modules. Every byte of it is generated.
gui/src-tauri/resources/
# A live orcode app home the dev loop writes into — never the owner's real
# one, and never a thing to commit.
gui/.devhome/
gui/preview-dist/
# `*.png` above is a blanket ignore for screenshots; the app's icons are
# generated build inputs and have to travel with the repo.
!gui/src-tauri/icons/*.png
